{"In handleNewBooking, evt.destinationCalendar is set to null when no destination calendar exists, causing optional chaining with push to silently skip adding teamDestinationCalendars for collective events": 0.7243490219116211, "GoogleCalendarService.updateEvent has incorrect fallback logic where selectedCalendar becomes undefined when externalCalendarId is not provided, because the fallback comparison uses the same falsy externalCalendarId value, causing Google Calendar API calls to fail": 0.9608877897262573, "LarkCalendarService, Office365CalendarService, and BaseCalendarService are missing the new credentialId parameter in createEvent, breaking the updated Calendar interface contract": 0.9153770804405212, "CalendarManager.createEvent changed the calendar API signature to require credentialId as second argument - this is a breaking change that may cause runtime mismatches if any calendar adapter was missed during refactor": 0.8210398554801941, "EventManager has been heavily refactored with new DB lookups introduced when iterating over destinationCalendar array, increasing complexity and potential performance issues": 0.20007455348968506, "Cancel handler's apiDeletes array mixes already-resolved values with raw Promises, and awaits the array itself rather than its contained promises, so deletion operations may never complete": 0.4004397690296173, "GoogleCalendarService.createEvent uses the first destinationCalendar element for organizer email regardless of which destination is being processed, potentially misattributing the organizer for non-first hosts": 0.903926432132721, "Async calls for cancelScheduledJobs and deleteScheduledReminder are fire-and-forget (unawaited) in forEach loops, meaning cleanup failures are silently ignored and may leave stale scheduled jobs": 0.06924701482057571, "teamDestinationCalendars array is mutated by pushing from inside an async map (teamMemberPromises), creating a potential race condition on shared array mutation": 0.1472903937101364}